---

Why AGPL-3.0 rather than a permissive license (deliberate choice, not a
default): unlike this project's companion library `@jobhakken/autofill`
(pure form-detection mechanics, MIT-licensed separately), this repository is
the product itself. AGPL-3.0 keeps the source open to contributors while
requiring that anyone who runs a modified version of this software as a
network service makes their modified source available to users of that
service — it is chosen specifically to prevent a closed-source competing
fork or hosted service built on this code without reciprocal contribution.
